  "slug": "cryo-em-1743",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and papers apply unsupervised autoencoders and diffusion models to cryo-EM/ET particle classification and tilt-series denoising.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the use of learned models to recover structural information from noisy, heterogeneous microscopy data. The unsupervised autoencoder preprint jointly optimizes particle pose and structure to classify cryo-EM and cryo-ET particles and to separate contamination. CryoET-DDM applies a diffusion model to denoise cryo-ET tilt series, drawing noise patches from the same tilt series and using a fidelity-guided loss to preserve underlying features. Both pair learned models with explicit constraints derived from the data itself. ROOF, a published method, is a semi-blind NMF approach to fluorescence bleed-through correction in multi-band microscopy, regularized by a reference crosstalk matrix. It falls outside cryo-EM but shares the emphasis on constrained decomposition of mixed imaging data. What is new is the explicit use of same-sample noise statistics and fidelity constraints to guide learned denoising and classification.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-14"
